{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1404826-thoughts-considerations-on-modeling-other-supernaturals-as-paradigms","id":1404826,"title":"Thoughts / Considerations on Modeling Other Supernaturals as Paradigms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-26T13:46:39-07:00","id":1404826,"title":"Thoughts / Considerations on Modeling Other Supernaturals as Paradigms","content":"Canon aside, do you think it would be possible to model other splats as sort of very restricted paradigms, given the new attention paid in M20 to paradigms. I know there was an original version book which had a sample NPC that thought they were a superhero.<br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> <br /> - Person who dies and comes back with sweet powers relating to Ghosts (Orpheus oWoD, Geist CoD)<br /> - Person who is a Changeling after being taken across the Hedge (Changeling CoD)<br /> etc<br /> <br /> I think the mechanic I'd need to figure out his how to make their magic more limited but less paradoxy to balance things out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T13:55:02-07:00","id":1404828,"title":"","content":"I could see modeling the Disciplines, Gifts, Arcanoi, etc. in this way. Inborn powers, such as a werewolf ability to shape-shift, could be modeled as Enhancements (which IMHO aren't a Technocracy-only thing), and weaknesses such as taking damage from sunlight could be handled as Echoes. <br /> <br /> So yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T14:32:43-07:00","id":1404833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1404826-thoughts-considerations-on-modeling-other-supernaturals-as-paradigms?p=1404828#post1404828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see modeling the Disciplines, Gifts, Arcanoi, etc. in this way. Inborn powers, such as a werewolf ability to shape-shift, could be modeled as Enhancements (which IMHO aren't a Technocracy-only thing), and weaknesses such as taking damage from sunlight could be handled as Echoes.<br /> So yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it. That's what I was looking for.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T13:40:24-07:00","id":1404969,"title":"","content":"Where are Enhancements and Echoes described. I couldn't find them in my M20 core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T21:49:19-07:00","id":1405019,"title":"","content":"Enhancements is a Background, usually used to describe a Technocrat with implants, biomods, or generic engineering; but it can be used to represent any beneficial inhuman trait, especially if it can be represented as an Effect. And upon reflection, you might not need Echoes after all; Enhancements come with built-in drawbacks that could be used to model the weaknesses that the likes of vampires and werewolves have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_